   342	- **D1. Per-library predicate vector and margins.** All ten predicates; hit, joint and boundary counts; exact mean biases. Count margins in targets: hits_d − 16 for each dimension, joint − 12, and 4 − boundary_d for each dimension (nine integers; a margin ≥ 0 means the count predicate is met). `min_count_margin` is the smallest of the nine, and `at_threshold` is true when any of the nine is 0. The bias margin, limit − |mean bias|, is an exact decimal string per dimension.
   343	- **D2. Target × library matrices (20 × 6).** Selected cell; joint hit; per-dimension hit; per-dimension identified flag; per-dimension boundary flag; global-tie flag; and the R = 12 re-profiled offset.
   344	- **D3. Per-target row summaries.** The number of libraries with a joint hit (0…6); the number with an offset hit; the number of distinct selected offsets; and `all_six_offsets_agree`, true if and only if all six R = 12 re-profiled offsets are non-null and equal. These show whether misses follow targets (rows) or libraries (columns).
