   346	  - The re-profiled offset per target under each of batches 1–4 (three replicates each), batches 1∪2 (six) and all twelve.
   347	  - Per fixed tuple, the range and median of the four batch objectives. The median is the arithmetic mean of the middle two of the four sorted values.
   348	  - The count of targets whose four batch offsets agree. **Agreement rule, stated here so that no brief has to add one (DIRECTOR lesson 2026-10-22, G37 F3):** a fit's re-profiled offset is the unique offset whose profiled objective lies within τ = 10⁻¹² · max(1, minimum profiled objective) of that minimum, or null if more than one does. Four batches agree if and only if all four re-profiled offsets are non-null and equal. A global numerical tie in a batch's fit does not by itself make the batch disagree. This is the rule as implemented and reviewed in G35-B (`_offset_descriptive`, `batch_offset_agreement`, `g35b_design_study.py:1202–1233` at `0c9c371`). D3's six-library flag uses the same rule.
