    49	## 2. Question, estimand and scope
    50	
    51	**Question.** At R = 12 candidate replicates per grid cell, does the frozen G35-B arm-(i) gate verdict, computed on one fresh shared target panel, depend on which independent candidate library was drawn?
    52	
    53	**Estimand.** For the frozen arm-(i) design the gate verdict is a function of two random draws: the candidate library (twelve process/observation pairs in four batches of three) and the target panel. This study holds the panel fixed and shared, and observes the verdict under L = 6 independently drawn libraries. The primary datum is **k**, the number of the six libraries whose frozen gate is PASS on the same N = 20 targets. The supporting data are the per-library predicate vectors and the target × library matrices (§7.9).
    54	
    55	**What is not estimated.** The observed count is `k` of six. The library pass probability on this panel remains unknown. The count is not a pass rate, not a reliability figure and not an interval, and no bound on that probability is reported.
    56	
    57	**Why the study is worth running where G41 was not.** The owner rejected G41 because one library is one draw of the thing that varies, and because neither outcome would have changed the next decision (ruling §3.1, §3.3). Here every reading class changes it:
    58	
    59	| Class (§7.3) | What Steven's next gate has in hand |
    60	|---|---|
    61	| CONSISTENT-PASS | No flip in six draws. Enough to ask whether a reliability study with its own ruled standard, or a second panel, is worth commissioning. Not enough to reopen anything. |
    62	| MIXED | A direct observation that the verdict changes with the library on identical targets. The "more replicates at R = 12" route is answered by measurement in place of an unknown. |
    63	| CONSISTENT-FAIL | No library reproduced recovery. The G35-B arm-(i) pass stands alone as a screening result. |
    64	| NO-READING | Nothing learned about library dependence; the cause is named. |
    65	
    66	**Design rules.**
    67	- One fixed campaign. No sequential or two-stage design, no early stopping at the first opposite pair.
    68	- No gated baseline, no gated R = 3 arm, no pooled gate, no combined factor.
    69	- G35-B results are lineage only. They are never pooled with G43 data: the targets differ, and the G35-B library was seen before this design.
    70	- Synthetic only. No real Jersey data enter. The frozen Jersey 2020 serosurvey table (`covid_serosurvey_2020`) is not read, imported or used. No serosurvey is modelled.
    71	- No horizon probe. The window is the frozen 30 days, so the only pre-freeze action on study seeds is the builds-only pre-check (§8).
    72	- Research harness only. Nothing is written through `CalibrationArtifactManifest` or `write_calibration_artifact`.
    73	
   148	### 7.1 Per-library recovery gate (brief item a)
   149	
   150	The G35-B predicates apply to each library separately, with N = 20 in place of 10.
   151	
   152	**Integer thresholds and their derivation.** The frozen ten-target counts are 8/10, 6/10 and ≤ 2/10. As fractions they are 4/5, 3/5 and 1/5. The frozen integer tests are hits·5 ≥ 4·N, joint·5 ≥ 3·N and boundary·5 ≤ 1·N. At N = 20:
   153	
   154	| Predicate | Frozen count at 10 | Fraction | Integer test at N = 20 | Count at 20 |
   155	|---|---:|---:|---|---:|
   156	| P5, per dimension | ≥ 8 | 4/5 | hits·5 ≥ 80 | **hits ≥ 16** |
   157	| P6, joint | ≥ 6 | 3/5 | joint·5 ≥ 60 | **joint ≥ 12** |
   158	| P8, per dimension | ≤ 2 | 1/5 | boundary·5 ≤ 20 | **boundary ≤ 4** |
   159	
   160	Equality at every inclusive endpoint qualifies. P7 divides the exact decimal sum of the twenty signed errors by 20. P2's "ten inoculation acquisitions" is the scenario's ten import attempts and does not scale with N.
   161	
   162	`G43 LIBRARY ℓ RECOVERY GATE: PASS` only if all of:
   163	1. All 20 target runs, all 625 candidate cells of library ℓ and all 12 replicates per cell complete without replacement.
   164	2. Each truth run realizes all ten inoculation acquisitions, at least one local secondary infection, reports in both channels, and at least three nonzero combined-report dates.
   165	3. Observation chronology and latent-incidence conservation pass for every truth run.
   166	4. No target has a numerically tied global minimum under library ℓ.
   167	5. Every dimension is identified and within tolerance for ≥ 16/20 targets.
   168	6. ≥ 12/20 targets are identified and within tolerance jointly in all four dimensions.
   169	7. Every dimension's absolute twenty-target mean bias is ≤ its limit (exact decimal). The mean is defined only when all twenty targets have a selected cell; otherwise the predicate is not met.
   170	8. No dimension is selected at an outermost grid value for more than 4/20 targets. This is computed by its own code path. On these grids every outermost value lies outside tolerance, so predicate 8 is implied by predicate 5; the per-dimension count is still reported.
   171	9. Seeds, namespaces, grid, objective, dates, fixed parameters, read-back and blind provenance match this declaration, and every build reproduces its frozen M2/M3/M4 logical hashes.
   172	10. Measured work equals the §9 caps: the shared-panel counts and library ℓ's own counts.
   173	
   174	**Status and failure rules (verbatim G35-B):**
   175	- `software_status` and `scientific_status` are kept separate.
   176	- An extinct or uninformative truth fails predicate 2 and is never resampled.
   177	- A poor or extinct candidate is scored.
   178	
   179	### 7.2 Three groups of predicates
   180	
   181	The frozen gate is a conjunction, and nothing here changes it. For the study-level reading the ten predicates are grouped by what they can depend on.
   182	
   183	| Group | Predicates | Depends on the candidate library? |
   184	|---|---|---|
   185	| **Shared-panel** | P2, P3, and the target-side components of P1 (20 target runs complete), P9 (target seeds, namespaces, truth cell, dates, fixed parameters, target build hashes) and P10 (shared-panel work counts) | No. Evaluated once on the shared panel; the same value enters all six gates. |
   186	| **Library-integrity** | the library-side components of P1 (625 cells × 12 replicates; 625 scored cells per target fit), P9 (library seeds, namespaces, read-back, blind provenance, candidate build hashes) and P10 (library work counts) | Yes, but they describe whether the work was done as declared, not whether recovery occurred. |
   187	| **Recovery** | P4, P5, P6, P7, P8 | Yes. These are the recovery criteria. |
   188	
   189	For library ℓ define two booleans:
   190	- `nonrecovery_ok_ℓ` = P1 ∧ P2 ∧ P3 ∧ P9 ∧ P10;
   191	- `recovery_met_ℓ` = P4 ∧ P5 ∧ P6 ∧ P7 ∧ P8.
   192	
   193	The gate verdict is PASS if and only if both are true, which is the frozen conjunction.
   194	
   590	## 9. Workload and fail-closed caps (brief item j)
   591	
   592	Each parent is built once per process seed. Each candidate latent run is reused across the 25 detection pairs. With L = 6 and N = 20:
   593	
   594	| Quantity | Shared panel | Per library | Formula | **Total** |
   595	|---|---:|---:|---|---:|
   596	| Builds | 20 | 12 | N + 12L | **92** |
   597	| Latent calls (30 days) | 20 | 12 × 25 = 300 | N + 300L | **1,820** |
   598	| Report transforms | 20 | 12 × 625 = 7,500 | N + 7,500L | **45,020** |
   599	| Candidate cells | — | 625 | 625L | **3,750** |
   600	| Gate loss evaluations | — | 625 × 20 = 12,500 | 625·N·L | **75,000** |
   601	| Gate blind records | — | 20 | N·L | **120** |
   602	| Descriptive loss evaluations (four batches + batches 1∪2) | — | 5 × 12,500 = 62,500 | 5·625·N·L | **375,000** |
   603	| Descriptive blind records | — | 5 × 20 = 100 | 5·N·L | **600** |
   604	| Serosurvey samples | 0 | 0 | — | **0** |
   605	
   606	The reference evaluations of §7.8 reuse the descriptive surfaces and add no loss evaluation.
   607	
   608	Predicate 10 reads the operational work ledger, including required descriptive scoring and record counts. Descriptive results and disclosure copies never feed P10 (§7.2, owner amendment A9).
   609	
   610	**Dry-run must enforce exact equality** to the Total column and to the shared and per-library columns separately:
   611	- builds 92 (20 + 6 × 12); latent calls 1,820 (20 + 6 × 300); transforms 45,020 (20 + 6 × 7,500);
   612	- 625 cells per library;
   613	- gate loss evaluations 75,000 and descriptive loss evaluations 375,000; blind records 120 and 600;
   614	- latent duration exactly 30 and calendar exactly 34 dates;
   615	- mode `ci`; serosurvey samples 0.
   616	
   617	It also rejects: seed overlap within the study or with any earlier set (§8); retries, replacement and adaptive work; any predicted or measured breach. Every call is reserved against its cap before dispatch, and an exception consumes its slot.
   618	
   619	**Outside the campaign.** The pre-check builds 138 process seeds: 20 targets + 10 target reserves + 72 candidates + 36 candidate reserves. It runs no latent call.
   620	
   621	**Wall time (unmeasured for this design; disclosure only, never a cap).** EXPLORATORY planning arithmetic from the G35-B `campaign_summary.json` arm-(i) disclosures (15.1 s for 9 builds, 215.9 s for 225 latent calls, 612.5 s for 5,625 transforms, 3.5 s scoring): about 1.7 s per build, 0.96 s per latent call and 0.11 s per transform. Scaling linearly, which is unreliable, gives roughly two hours, plus scoring and retention I/O that were not measured at this scale. The campaign records per-phase `time.perf_counter()` totals (build, latent, transform, scoring, retention) for the shared panel and for each library, and every latent call's `runtime_seconds`. **All wall-time figures come from one source,** `campaign_summary.json.disclosures`; any per-library disclosure file copies them byte-for-byte or omits them (exit-audit O1).
   622	
   623	**Retained size and host disk (unmeasured; estimate).**
   624	- The bundle holds about 45,000 candidate table files, 20 target tables, 720 blind records and the latent-truth files: of the order of 46,000–47,000 files.
   625	- EXPLORATORY estimate: 0.5–1 GB. It is scaled from the G35-B arm-(i) directory and has no precision.
   626	- The disk used by 92 retained or transient parent builds, and the peak memory of holding one library's latent results, are **unknown**. U3 measures both on a non-study seed (§13) and the director adds them to the estimate before asking Steven for the campaign.
   627	- **Host-disk rule (DIRECTOR lesson 2026-09-02).** The bundle is written inside the WSL VHD, which grows on the Windows host drive. Before launch the director checks `df /mnt/c` and logs it. The launcher refuses to start unless host free space is at least 5 GB plus the upper size estimate as updated by U3's measurement. The measured bundle size is disclosed afterwards.
   628	

